  "answer_text": "It looks like the **2026 NBA Finals** are currently underway, with the **New York Knicks vs. San Antonio Spurs**! Here's where you can get tickets:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc0 Next NBA Finals Game\nThe New York Knicks currently hold a 2-0 series lead against the San Antonio Spurs in the 2026 NBA Finals. The next games in the series are coming up soon.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf9f\ufe0f Where to Buy Tickets\n\n1. **Ticketmaster** *(Official NBA Ticketing Partner)*\n   - NBA tickets for the 2025-2026 season are available to purchase on Ticketmaster, the Official Ticketing Partner of the NBA.\n   - Visit: [ticketmaster.com/nba](https://www.ticketmaster.com/nba)\n   - If tickets for a game are sold out, additional seats may become available closer to the game, so keep checking back.\n\n2. **NBA.com**\n   - The official NBA schedule page at NBA.com lists all upcoming games, including playoffs, and has a tickets section.\n   - Visit: [nba.com/schedule](https://www.nba.com/schedule)\n\n3. **AmericanArenas.com**\n   - NBA Finals tickets for 2026 start at $1,009 \u2014 you can compare ticket prices and explore upcoming NBA Finals games through the season.\n   - Visit: [americanarenas.com/tickets/nba-finals](https://americanarenas.com/tickets/nba-finals/)\n\n4. **NBATickets.us**\n   - This site offers NBA tickets and VIP packages for current and upcoming games.\n   - Visit: [nbatickets.us](https://nbatickets.us/)\n\n5. **ESPN**\n   - ESPN has a complete 2026 NBA season schedule that includes game times, TV listings, and ticket information for all NBA games.\n   - Visit: [espn.com/nba/schedule](https://www.espn.com/nba/schedule)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips\n- Ticket prices for NBA games depend on a variety of factors, including date and time, city, matchup, and seat location. The average ticket for an NBA game can cost anywhere between $100\u2013$200 \u2014 though **Finals tickets will be significantly higher**.\n- Plan to leave at least an hour before tip-off to allow time to park, get through security, find your seats, and maybe even catch the pre-game warm-ups.",
